        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "124d555e-91a3-5e20-951e-62d85a5fffa5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Columbia River, Oregon, Washington, Palm Beach County, Florida, Tanner Creek\n- Projects: Cascade Locks and Canal, Oregon Portage Railroad\n- Buildings: The Breakers, Royal Poinciana Hotel\n- Water bodies: Lake Worth Lagoon\n- Systems: Bonneville Dam\n- People: Henry Flagler\n\nFacts:\n- In 1894, Henry Flagler opened the Royal Poinciana Hotel beside Lake Worth Lagoon facing the inland waterway.\n- In 1896, the Cascade Locks and Canal was completed as a navigation project on the Columbia River between Oregon and Washington.\n- During the later years of the Oregon Portage Railroad's operation, the railroad ran from Tanner Creek, near the future site of Bonneville Dam, to the Cascade Locks while the locks were under construction.\n- Lake Worth Lagoon is a lagoon in Palm Beach County, Florida.\n- The Breakers occupies the beachfront portion of the former grounds of the Royal Poinciana Hotel.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f6f62864-5494-5c33-a618-fc69083b2234",
